      "text": "<!-- PDF_PAGE: 2 -->\n## PDF page 2 — printed page 2\n\nTHE EXAMPLE GAZETTE. 2\n\n### TO OUR READERS (continued from page 1)\n\nThe new plan will allow room for longer reports from the townships, and for the market prices, which many have asked for. The subscription remains two dollars a year. — THE EDITOR.\n\n### AROUND THE COUNTY (continued)\n\n#### Riverton\n\nThe ferry resumed its crossings on the 12th, the river having fallen. A new landing is talked of. — R. R.\n\n#### Lakeside\n\nThe ice went out of the lake on April 9, nine days later than last year. — A CORRESPONDENT.\n\n---\n\n### THE NEW BRIDGE\n\nThe county commissioners met on Wednesday to open the bids for the iron bridge over the Mill River. Four bids were received, the lowest from a firm in Springfield.\n\n*(continued on page 6)*\n\n",
